<title>ITALY: Italy's Bari sees April CPI at 0.0 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Bari sees April CPI at 0.0 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>BARI, Italy 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Bari said its April consumer price index stood at 0.0 percent month on month and 1.3 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In March, Bari's inflation rate fell 0.2 percent monthly and rose 1.8 percent year on year.</p>
<p>Bari is one of 11 Italian cities to publish inflation data on Monday and Tuesday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 5.99 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to March 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.0   (-0.2)    1.3    (1.8)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.2   (-0.1)   -0.4    (0.2)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.2    (0.0)    1.1    (1.9)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges  -0.3    (0.2)    2.5    (6.1)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0   (-0.1)    1.3    (1.5)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.1   (-0.3)    3.1    (3.5)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.0    (0.3)    5.8    (6.2)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -0.1   (-1.1)   -0.8   (-0.6)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0    (0.0)    3.5    (3.9)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.1   (-0.8)    0.7    (0.6)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.0    (0.0)    0.8    (0.7)</p>
<p>-- Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
